  "num_turns": null,
  "final_message": "I fixed the off-by-one bug in `paginate.py`, and `python3 -m unittest -v test_public.py` now passes (1 test, OK).\n\n**The bug:** pages are 1-indexed, but `paginate.py:8` calculated `start = page * page_size`. That skipped a whole page, so page 1 returned `[3, 4]` instead of `[1, 2]`.\n\n**The fix:** that line is now `start = (page - 1) * page_size`, the same formula `page_bounds` already uses. I didn't touch `total_pages` or `page_bounds`, as the README asks.\n\nI also tried a few more pages on `[1,2,3,4,5]` with a page size of 2: page 2 gives `[3, 4]`, page 3 gives `[5]`, and page 4 gives `[]`.\n\nDONE: Fixed paginate's start offset to (page - 1) * page_size so pages are 1-indexed; public test passes.",
